title: Setup guide
---
body:

This guide gets you ready to run the course marimo notebooks in VS Code using a reproducible **pixi** environment.

#### Install pixi
- Follow the installation instructions at <https://pixi.sh/latest/>.

#### Install VS Code
- Download and install from <https://code.visualstudio.com/>.

#### Download the course materials
- Direct download (recommended): <https://github.com/yoavram/ModelsPopBiol/archive/refs/heads/master.zip>
  - Unzip and note the folder path (e.g., `~/Downloads/ModelsPopBiol-master`).
- If you prefer `git`, clone <https://github.com/yoavram/ModelsPopBiol> (not covered here).

#### Open the course folder in VS Code
- Start VS Code in the course folder: **File → Open Folder…** → select the course folder.

#### Install the Python extension for VS Code
- Open VS Code → Extensions → search **Python** (by Microsoft) → Install.
- Reference: <https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/python/python-quick-start>

#### Optional: Install the Jupyter extension for VS Code
- Extensions → search **Jupyter** (by Microsoft) → Install only if you still need to open legacy `.ipynb` notebooks.
- Reference: <https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/datascience/jupyter-notebooks>


#### Create the course environment from the VS Code terminal
- In VS Code: **Terminal → New Terminal**. Confirm the terminal path is the course folder (the one containing `pixi.lock`).
- Run:
  ```bash
  pixi install --locked
  ```

#### Open marimo notebooks
- Run marimo from the VS Code terminal:
  ```bash
  pixi run marimo edit notebooks/population-growth.py
  ```
- You can open other course notebooks by replacing the file name with another notebook in `notebooks/*.py`.

#### Quick test
In the VS Code terminal, run:
```bash
pixi run python -c "import numpy; print(numpy.__version__)"
```
You should see version number without errors.

#### Enable GitHub Copilot in VS Code
- Apply or sign in at <https://education.github.com/pack> to get Copilot Pro for free.
- Set up **GitHub Copilot** in VS Code: <https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/copilot/setup>
